# URL CW-factor author-code acquisition v1

## Question

Does the source-linked author archive contain an executable implementation of
the published diagonal-plus-low-rank CW update, with enough definition to plan
a native small-day calibration without reconstructing the method from prose?

## Bounded action

Download only `cw_fa_code.tar.gz` from the UCSD maintainer page, compute its
SHA-256 and size, reject unsafe archive members, extract it under `.deps`, and
record the member inventory and hashes.  Do not download the 234 MB URL data in
this task and do not execute code from the archive.

The archive and extracted code have no explicit license located in the source
page, so they remain recoverable local `.deps` material and are excluded from
the persistent checkpoint.  Only the manifest is persistent.

## Outcomes

- If the archive is unavailable, retain the exact URL/error and continue with a
  prose-derived implementation only after deciding whether that loss of native
  code provenance is acceptable.
- If it contains the published update and data interfaces, audit equations,
  dependencies and array shapes before downloading native data.
- If it is synthetic-only or lacks the URL path, record that limitation; do not
  call a rewritten implementation an author-code reproduction.
